divergence: this program uses `Db.Decode.money`, which returns `Decoder (Decimal, String)` in the Rust backend versus `Decoder Money` in the Go backend (backlog #34 / class7-sql-db-fix-spec-2026-07-09.md S6 "API-shape decision"). Go's runtime is dynamically typed and can construct an arbitrary `Money` ADT at runtime; the Rust runtime cannot name project-generated `Money`/`Currency` types from the shared crate, so it returns the structural `(Decimal, String)` pair instead. This Main.ipe's `\( amount, code ) -> ...` tuple-pattern lambda would not even type-check against the Go backend's `Decoder Money` shape, so a shared Main.ipe cannot run identically on both backends. Ipê's output is recorded as the reference for this Rust-specific surface. Also uses other Std.Db kernels (Db.open / Db.withTransaction / Db.exec / Db.queryDecode) already covered by the pre-existing Db backend divergence.
